<title>HONG KONG: NatWest sets warrants on HK finance basket.</title>
<headline>NatWest sets warrants on HK finance basket.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>NatWest Financial Products Plc said on Tuesday it has launched 439 million American-style call warrants on a basket of red- and blue-chip finance stocks.</p>
<p>The basket comprises of:</p>
<p> HSBC Holdings Ltd		 0.01 shares</p>
<p> Ka Wah Bank Ltd		   0.18 shares</p>
<p> FPB Bank Holdings Ltd	   0.2  shares</p>
<p> Union Bank of Hong Kong Ltd   0.056 shares</p>
<p>Ten warrants control one basket.</p>
<p> STRIKE PRICE	 HK$4.5279   PREMIUM	 12.7 PCT</p>
<p> ISSUE PRICE	  HK$0.1142   GEARING	 4.4x</p>
<p> EXPIRATION	   03.APR.98   MIN EXER LOT  10,000</p>
<p> REFERENCE SPOT     HK$5.031    LISTING DATE  25.JUN.97</p>
<p> LISTING		HONG KONG   PAY DATE	24.JUN.97</p>
<p> GOVERNING LAW	ENGLISH</p>
<p> NOTE		   ISSUER'S CASH OPTION AT THE HIGHER OF THE</p>
<p>			  AVERAGE CLOSING PRICE OF THE SHARES FOR THE</p>
<p>			  30 BUSINESS DAYS IMMEDIATELY BEFORE THE</p>
<p>			  EXPIRY DATE OR THE CLOSING PRICE OF THE</p>
<p>			  SHARES ON THE DAY BEFORE THE EXPIRY DATE.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6441.  http://www.hk97.com</p>
</text>
